# BigQuery profile (optional — enable when using cloud)

Copy to `%USERPROFILE%\.dbt\profiles.yml` or merge as a second target `bigquery`.

```yaml
github_archive:
  target: local
  outputs:
    local:
      type: duckdb
      path: data/github_archive.duckdb
      threads: 4

    bigquery:
      type: bigquery
      method: service-account
      project: "{{ env_var('GCP_PROJECT_ID') }}"
      dataset: github_archive_dbt
      threads: 4
      timeout_seconds: 300
      location: US
      keyfile: "{{ env_var('GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_PATH') }}"
```

Switch target: `dbt run --target bigquery`

Staging SQL for BigQuery uses nested fields (`actor.login`, `JSON_VALUE`, `SAFE_OFFSET`) — see `docs/bigquery_staging_snippets.md`.
